<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tuanku Abdul Rahman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1895–1960</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tuanku Abdul Rahman was the Yang di-Pertuan Besar, or ruler, of Negeri Sembilan from 1933 and the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yang-di-pertuan-agong">Yang di-Pertuan Agong</a>, the elected supreme head of state, of the Federation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malaya">Malaya</a>. Chosen by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conference-of-rulers">Conference of Rulers</a>, he took office at independence in 1957 and served until his death in 1960. His portrait has appeared on every series of Malaysian banknotes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tuanku-abdul-rahman.jpg" alt="Tuanku Abdul Rahman" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymity · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HRH_Tuanku_Abdul_Rahman_Ibni_Al-Marhum_Tuanku_Muhammad._The_Tuanku_Ja%27afar_Royal_Gallery,_Seremban.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
